# v1.14 P3 PR review — live progress view — REVISED after your blockers

This is the revised diff for the PR you reviewed (unanimous SHIP WITH CHANGES, 2 blockers + a Codex ship-gate + optional O3). Every item is addressed, plus the independent finder's one MINOR (same root as your O3). Confirm cleared or name what still fails with file:line. SHIP = mergeable; the v1.14.0 release follows one phase later.

## Your items → resolutions
1. **Artifact tree lies under --no-live-status (your #1):** fixed exactly as you prescribed — resolved `live_status: bool` on RunConfig (set from `not args.no_live_status`, mirroring `endorse`), the single source of truth for the cli wiring AND `render_artifact_tree(config)`, which now gates the status line like every sibling optional slot. Deliberately NOT persisted in the recipe (presentation flag for a non-record artifact — the `--strict-exit`/`--digest-format` convention, unlike `endorse` which changes record-artifact presence; rationale comment at the recipe field-selection site, answering your open question #2). Tests: the tree-omission test you named + a dry-run `--no-live-status` E2E asserting no status.* in the preview.
2. **RH-1 prose overclaims (your #2):** resolved in your Claude seat's direction (behavior preserved, docs corrected — the refusal-manifest behavior is pre-existing and test-asserted): all four sites (CHANGELOG, SKILL.md, scripts/README.md, status.py docstring) now read "preflight NO-GO leaves no dir; an egress-refused run writes only the refusal manifest (egress-manifest.md + sensitivity.json), never status.*". New E2E locks the true invariant (manifest present, status.* absent).
3. **Malformed status readers (Codex's ship-gate):** `event_tuples` and `render_status_html` now isinstance-guard doc/seats/events containers and skip/normalize malformed entries (house guard style); a malformation matrix test proves no raw tracebacks. Note: no CLI surface READS a status.json (it is conductor-write-only), so the exit-2 clause has no applicable site — the hardening covers both actual readers.
4. **O3 / abort-refresh (also the independent finder's MINOR):** the post-activate run body is now wrapped try/finally — any abnormal exit (the mid-fan-out `die()` drift guards, KeyboardInterrupt, unhandled exception) stamps `finished` with new outcome constant `interrupted` via idempotent `finish_if_unfinished()` (best-effort: a failing stamp never masks the original exception; exit codes and die() messages re-raise untouched — test-asserted) and re-renders the html STATIC (no meta-refresh). Seats keep their honest last-known states. Tests: mid-fan-out die() variant + KeyboardInterrupt variant.

## State
Suite: **1426 OK** (+7 over your review's 1419; 1404 at the P2 baseline), verified by an independent full run. Thread-safety, RH-1 code behavior, byte-drift-zero, torn-read atomicity, and best-effort-under-failure were all probed clean by the independent finder last round (hammer probe: 4801/4801 events, monotonic seq, zero torn reads) and are untouched except as described.

